. She was totally absorbed in the domestic duties of Geeka – so much so that she did not note the gentle swaying of the branches of the tree above her as they bent to the body of the creature that had entered them stealthily from the jungle.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["engage","engross","immerse","monopolize","occupy"],"antonyms":["emit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["absorbability","absorbable","absorbance","absorbate","absorbefacient","absorbent","absorb oneself in","absorption","absorptive","bioabsorb","misabsorb","overabsorb","preabsorb","reabsorb","X-ray absorbing glass"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absorb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a0fb65549c15ab7f13","definition":"To occupy or consume time.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["use up"],"antonyms":["emit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["absorbability","absorbable","absorbance","absorbate","absorbefacient","absorbent","absorb oneself in","absorption","absorptive","bioabsorb","misabsorb","overabsorb","preabsorb","reabsorb","X-ray absorbing glass"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absorb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:45fda064410978bf70","definition":"To assimilate mentally.","example":"If we fail to absorb the lessons of history, we are doomed to repeat them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bear","pay for","take in"],"antonyms":["emit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["absorbability","absorbable","absorbance","absorbate","absorbefacient","absorbent","absorb oneself in","absorption","absorptive","bioabsorb","misabsorb","overabsorb","preabsorb","reabsorb","X-ray absorbing glass"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary con